						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, June 04, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">To low for Destiny is now recruiting! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hey all of Norrath! How are you, sad were all to low for destiny? Well im putting together a guild to express ourselve, lol. Seriousily though, if you are interested in making this guild a good guild we could make a great guild. We could have a very organized infostructure as well as a great roster so if you wanna join send me an email at Johnrev2007@aol.com
							<br><BR>
							 - Vanna<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=279">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, May 31, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Luclin's Descendants Up! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hail Fellow Norrathians! Solusek Ro has yet another new guild out and about. We are Luclin's Descendants. No level range as of yet, so send Stunch or Zhanzarist a tell in game if your interested. Were a guild looking to defy traditional guild rules,and go against the grain. E-mail ForestFrog59@aol.com if your interested in joining our ranks. Good hunting!<BR>Zhanzarist<BR>Luclin's Descendants<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Zhanzarist<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=278">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, May 27, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Death Ro RAID Organization </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Attention Guilds: Syndicate Ro is forming a Raiding Organization known as Death Ro. Our guild has around 100 members primarly levels 15-35 and we will be conducting many raids for mid-level characters.<BR><BR>I am offering an alliance to interested guilds who would like to help organize and raid with us. If interested email me.<BR><BR>Prince Venefix<BR>venefix@eqsyndicate.com<BR>www.eqsyndicate.com
							<br><BR>
							 - venefix<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=277">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, May 21, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">New project. </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Team "Spartans" invites all characters level 56+ to participate in our new project:<BR><BR>Guild "ENIGMA" is currently in the development. To learn more please go to<BR><BR>http://www.geocities.com/enigmasolro<BR><BR>If you are interested and would like to participate or have any questions contact me in game. <BR><BR>Flaor McLife, 59 shaman<BR>alt: Enjolras Justicar, 52 magician
							<br><BR>
							 - Flaor<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=275">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=275">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">100+ Members Now! </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							Syndicate Ro was implemented in game just a couple months ago, and we have reached over 100 members today. Check us out at www.eqsyndicate.com, we are looking for more! No level restrictions, so look us up today. We have been praised for our unique ideas and great website.<BR><BR>At our site you get control of your own personal page, complete with bio, level, photo, and more.<BR><BR>Our site features a map of Norrath including numbers on the map showing how many of our members are where! Search for Syndicates by race, class, and more. With a click of the button you'll know where all the clerics are, etc.<BR><BR>New feature: SYNDICATE AWARDS. By honoring the guild and your guildmates you can now earn awards which will be posted on your personal pages.<BR><BR>Visit www.eqsyndicate.com to join our empire on Solusek Ro.
							 <BR><BR>- venefix<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=274">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, May 20, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">New address </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							New site address for Avalanche Of Power at http://aop.sytes.net/index.html.<BR><BR>Also we have begun using a new messgage board (link to it located upon at the new site address)
							<br><BR>
							 - Eldera<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=273">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=273">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Sunday, May 12, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">RISING LEGACY </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Rising Legacy has formed, we now have a web site up.  Although it's not finished, I wanted to share the good news.  We still have the guild charter, pledge rules, etc. to sort out.  As well as finishing off the site and creating a decent forum (tempory EZboard up).<BR><BR>Come and say hello, friends and strangers welcome alike.  Our site won't be hosted on geocities forever either. :)<BR><BR>http://www.geocities.com/scurveypestilential/
							<br><BR>
							 - Scurvey Pestilential<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=270">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=270">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, May 03, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Ring of Honor Implemented </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							As of April 20th, a great meeting of guilds throughout our beloved server met to discuss coming together for a common purpose: To uphold honor and help out each other in many encounters.  Thus was born the Ring of Honor, consisting of the following guilds:<BR>Blades of Light<BR>Gathered Might<BR>Dog Soldiers<BR>Clan Donald<BR>Sacred Honor<BR>Battle Forged<BR>The Blood Sworn<BR><BR>This is not a merging of all of these guilds, but rather a Ring of friendship, and fellowship with many like minded individuals.<BR><BR>We also have a calendar at http://www.calsnet.net/rohcalendar <BR><BR>Please visit this calendar as since we have many guilds and many raids, we would want to try to avoid any conflicts with any other citizens of Norrath in our endeavors.<BR><BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Calenon<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=269">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, April 29, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">The Gnome's Revolt </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							It begins...<BR><BR>All through the night you tossed and turned, waking on occasion you vaguely remember the dream that seems to be causing your restlessness. Now, the steam whistles are piping their discordant wake-up calls, the days work has begun in the factories and tunnels of Ak'Anon.<BR><BR>Rise and groan. Get dressed. Open the door and head to your work cubby with maps and blueprints tucked under your arm.<BR><BR><BR>You will regret your lack of sleep later today. Nevermind that, you regret it now! One of your associates is coming towards you with what looks like yesterdays papers that you had completed, and he doesn't look happy. His yelling and shouting is lost to the banging and clanging of the nearby machinery. Upon further inspection of your work you don't see where there is a problem. He insists that it's wrong though, so you decide to rework it today before lunch.<BR><BR><BR>You look up and notice sweat starting to bead up on his brow. He is standing in the same spot where he was yelling at you 10 minutes ago. Then, suddenly, he collapses in a heap on the floor.<BR><BR><BR>You rush over to him to find that he is indeed alive, but is unconscious. <BR><BR><BR>"Cleric!!", you yell. "We need a Cleric!", and the rest is a blur.<BR><BR>To be continued... <BR><BR>For more information please Check out The <a href=http://home.earthlink.net/~shadowintheattic/GnomeRevoltPreview.htm target=_TOP>Gathered Might </a> Web Page
							<br><BR>
							 - Gharret Ardere<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=268">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, April 25, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">WHOAH! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hey look! A NEW SSOTW! :)<BR><BR>Yes it has taken a long time to get that thing changes. Both Ganza and I have been pretty busy with RL and leveling sometimes of course.<BR><BR><BR>As Far as the news section, please use it for World EQ news, and Sol Ro info like Guild events or any NEWS event you think we need to have :) Please do not post FOR SALE or gripes about players in the news, it will not get approved.<BR><BR><BR>As for the new mail accounts that have to be added, about 400+ atm, we have been capped somehow by the hosting company. We are currently working on something to get that fixed. <BR><BR><BR>Also, we are working on some new things here at the SolRo site. Taking ideas, so far we have a couple like a PRICE CHECK section for up to the day prices on select items on ONLY SolRo, a searchable database of the users on this site to see current levels and such, Adding some fields in the user profile to actually keep records of where your skills are etc... <BR><BR><BR>If you have any more cool ideas, please email Anumatu at anumatu@solusekro.com or Ganza at ganza@solusekro.com<BR><BR><BR>Would also like to thank Adrastea for he continued help with the GUILDS section of the site. I believe with her help we have the best list of guilds on the server.<BR><BR><BR>Everyone should know that you can edit your profile at any time to change your info, except for name of course. So if you feel up to it UPDATE! :P<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Anumatu<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=266">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=266">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>

